  Reading:
   * capture near CEILING phase  -> model ceiling odd term has the RIGHT sign, just
     too big -> a ceiling-magnitude reshape can work.
   * capture near CLIPPER phase  -> model ceiling odd term is BACKWARDS -> magnitude
     tweak cannot fix it; a phase-aware fit target is mandatory.
   * verdict DIFFERING across (clean) tones = the nonlinear H3 phase is
     FREQUENCY-DEPENDENT -> direct evidence for the static-vs-dynamic test (step 2).

